    "id": "Youmu76/jingzhang-protocol-belt",
    "slug": "jingzhang-protocol-belt",
    "title": "京张协议带 JINGZHANG PROTOCOL BELT：把 AI 城市设计写成可审计的公共协议",
    "titleEn": "JINGZHANG PROTOCOL BELT: Writing AI Urban Design as an Auditable Public Protocol",
    "summary": "以「京张协议」为制度内核，把百年京张铁路的自主标准精神转译为城市级 AI 公共协议实验场：一脉（9公里绿脉协议脊）、三信标（众智园可信算力信标/原点开源协议信标/大钟寺人机共处信标）、两翼（中关村科技服务翼/小月河场景赋能翼）、五处缝合道口与十二个协议场景节点。方案反写主流叙事——不是问 AI 能给这条带带来什么，而是问这条带如何约束 AI：每个 AI 场景落地都须签署公开协议（数据最小化/可回退/人类复核/收益共享），以詹天佑「人」字形线路为元符号，把「折返式治理」写进空间。全部几何基于 provisional boundary 生成，官方 polygon 发布后整包重算。",
    "summaryEn": "With the Jing-Zhang Protocol as its institutional core, this proposal translates the century-old spirit of indigenous standards in the Beijing-Zhangjiakou Railway into a city-scale AI public protocol laboratory: one spine (9km green protocol ridge), three beacons (Zhongzhiyuan trusted-compute beacon / AI Origin open-source protocol beacon / Dazhongsi human-AI coexistence beacon), two wings (Zhongguancun technology-service wing / Xiaoyuehe scenario-empowerment wing), five stitch crossings and twelve protocol scenario nodes. It inverts the mainstream narrative — not 'what AI can bring to the belt', but 'how the belt constrains AI': every AI deployment must sign a public protocol (data minimization / rollback / human review / benefit sharing), using Zhan Tianyou's chevron (人-shaped) alignment as the meta-symbol to inscribe 'switchback governance' into space. All geometry is generated on the provisional boundary and fully recalculated when official polygons are released.",
