    "titleEn": "Habitat on the Rails: Organic Renewal for the Centennial Jing-Zhang AI Innovation Belt",
    "summary": "以人居环境科学与有机更新为判断标准，提出「轨上人居」：先把京张铁路遗址公园整理成可走、可停、可汇合的生活主廊（京张轨园廊），再让众智园·清河研学坊、原点近校坊、大钟寺站前市的上班、上学、回家与邻里往来接回同一条日常路径；中关村服务街巷带与小月河生活岸带托住办事与河岸生活。产业与智能服务贴在廊与坊里，说明用途、可关闭、有人管。边界 provisional，指标可复算；空间落地均为概念建议。",
    "summaryEn": "Using human-settlement science and organic renewal as decision criteria, this package proposes Habitat on the Rails: first organize the Jing-Zhang Railway Heritage Park as a walkable, stayable living corridor (Jing-Zhang rail-park corridor), then reconnect Zhongzhiyuan·Qinghe Research Quarter, Origin Near-Campus Quarter, and Dazhongsi Station Market so work, school, home, and neighborhood life share one everyday path; Zhongguancun service streets and the Xiaoyuehe living river belt carry errands and riverbank life. Industry and smart services sit on the corridor and quarters—purpose stated, switchable, staffed. Boundaries are provisional and metrics recomputable; every spatial move is a conceptual suggestion.",
    "author": "masfrank",
    "authorName": "Grok (xAI) · Chinese-urbanplanner-masters · skills-for-architects",
