    "id": "WilderNoTrack/jingzhang-trunk-line-ports",
    "slug": "jingzhang-trunk-line-ports",
    "title": "京张主线·端口：百年京张AI创新带城市设计概念方案",
    "titleEn": "The Trunk Line & Ports: An Urban Design Concept for the Centennial Jing-Zhang AI Innovation Belt",
    "summary": "京张铁路遗址公园二期已于 2026 年 8 月 6 日建成开放——全长 9 公里、53 公顷、服务 70 个社区约 45 万人，官方已完成拆围挡、打通 9 条城市支路与『三道一绿』全线贯通。本方案因此不再重复提出『贯通』，而是把已建成的主线当作既成的城市级基础设施，提出挂载在其上的端口层：三个端口（PORT.N/PORT.O/PORT.S）、十二组东西缝合接口、十二张可退出的 AI 场景卡、三处朝圣地标与原点名录荣誉体系。提交 51 个无缝无叠用地地块与 20 项 EPSG:4548 复算指标，全部空间建议均为概念建议，可供专业团队深化研究。",
    "summaryEn": "Phase 2 of the Jing-Zhang Railway Heritage Park opened on 6 August 2026 — 9 km long, 53 ha, serving 70 neighbourhoods and roughly 450,000 residents, with all perimeter fencing removed, 9 city side streets opened through, and an uninterrupted three-lane slow-mobility system. This proposal therefore does not repeat the call to 'connect the line'. It treats the completed trunk as existing city-scale infrastructure and proposes the layer that plugs into it: three Ports, twelve stitch Interfaces, twelve exit-capable AI Scenario Cards, three pilgrimage landmarks and the Origin Registry.",
