    "slug": "chevron-line",
    "title": "人字线 The Chevron Line：百年京张AI创新带城市设计概念方案",
    "titleEn": "The Chevron Line — Centennial Jing-Zhang AI Innovation Belt. Subtitle: Two Legs, One Climb.",
    "summary": "以京张遗址公园为南北贯通的主脊，在五个位置用“人”字形的东西向缝合臂把被铁路走廊分开的两侧街区重新接上，三处重点区域各承担一组功能，两翼向中关村与小月河外接。全部空间结论可由提交的 GeoJSON 与 metrics.json 在 EPSG:4548 下复算；官方红线、控规条件、文保控制线与现状普查数据缺失部分一律标记为待补，不做推算。成果为概念建议与参考方案，可供专业团队深化研究。",
    "summaryEn": "With Jing-Zhang Heritage Park as the north-south spine, use \\\"person\\\" shaped east-west stitches at five positions to reconnect the two sides of the neighborhood divided by the railway corridor. Three key areas each carry a set of functions, with the wings extending to Zhongguancun and Xiao Yuehe. All spatial conclusions can be recalculated using the submitted GeoJSON and metrics.json under EPSG:4548; official planning boundaries, control conditions, cultural heritage control lines, and missing parts of the current census data should be marked as pending and not estimated. The results are a Conceptual Recommendation and reference plan, available for professional teams to deepen their research. (Official Planning Boundary)",
